\title{breedtools: design, analysis and 'Breedbase' storage of plant breeding trials}
\description{
breedtools designs and analyses plant breeding field trials, from early
generations with a single plot per entry to fully replicated trials, and
saves the designs into a 'Breedbase' database. The tutorial,
\code{vignette("breedtools")}, walks through every design and analysis.
}
\section{Which design?}{

\itemize{
\item One plot per entry, one location: augmented row-column design
with replicated checks.
\item One plot per entry per location, several locations: augmented
partially replicated (p-rep) design, without checks.
\item Every entry in every replicate: resolvable (spatial) row-column
design.
}
}

\section{Augmented row-column designs}{

Unreplicated entries plus replicated checks in rows, columns and blocks
(Federer, Nair and Raghavarao, 1975; Piepho and Williams, 2016), with
equal or unequal row and column groups, complete or incomplete blocks of
checks, and Latin or D-optimal check placement that keeps checks apart.
\itemize{
\item Plan: \code{\link[=augmented_row_column_layouts]{augmented_row_column_layouts()}}, \code{\link[=augmented_row_column_capacity]{augmented_row_column_capacity()}}
\item Design: \code{\link[=augmented_row_column_design]{augmented_row_column_design()}}
\item Map: \code{\link[=plot_augmented_row_column_design]{plot_augmented_row_column_design()}}
\item Analysis (fixed, random blocks, random entries, SpATS spatial):
\code{\link[=analyze_augmented_row_column_design]{analyze_augmented_row_column_design()}}
}
}

\section{Augmented p-rep designs}{

Multi-location trials in which a share of the entries is repeated at each
location (Williams, Piepho and Whitaker, 2011), built by search or from
alpha and alpha(2) arrays.
\itemize{
\item Plan: \code{\link[=augmented_prep_parameters]{augmented_prep_parameters()}}
\item Design: \code{\link[=augmented_prep_design]{augmented_prep_design()}}, \code{\link[=augmented_prep_concurrence]{augmented_prep_concurrence()}}
\item Map: \code{\link[=plot_augmented_prep_design]{plot_augmented_prep_design()}}
\item Analysis (with replicates and fixed or random genotype x location):
\code{\link[=analyze_augmented_prep_design]{analyze_augmented_prep_design()}}
\item Two-stage weighted analysis with block or SpATS spatial stage 1:
\code{\link[=analyze_augmented_prep_two_stage]{analyze_augmented_prep_two_stage()}}
}
}

\section{Resolvable row-column designs}{

Fully replicated designs optimized for row-column and spatial (linear
variance) efficiency, with latinized options (Williams, John and
Whitaker, 2006).
\itemize{
\item Design: \code{\link[=resolvable_row_column_design]{resolvable_row_column_design()}}
\item Efficiency, neighbours, AR criterion: \code{\link[=resolvable_row_column_efficiency]{resolvable_row_column_efficiency()}}
\item Map: \code{\link[=plot_resolvable_row_column_design]{plot_resolvable_row_column_design()}}
\item Analysis (RC, LV + RC and AR + RC by REML): \code{\link[=analyze_resolvable_row_column]{analyze_resolvable_row_column()}}
}
